<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 191 0 R
/T (Thus the virtues of Ramadan are not merely theological facts to be admired; they are invitations to respond. The gates are opened so that one may enter. The rewards are multiplied so that one may strive. The night is elevated so that one may seek it. The mercy is near so that one may return.)
/E (Thus the virtues of Ramadan are not merely theological facts to be admired; they are invitations to respond. The gates are opened so that one may enter. The rewards are multiplied so that one may strive. The night is elevated so that one may seek it. The mercy is near so that one may return.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
