443 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Seeking Laylat al-Qadr across multiple nights trains consistency rather than emotional dependency. It teaches the believer that transformation is rarely a sudden illumination; more often it is the fruit of repeated turning, of standing night after night even when concentration fluctuates. Not every night will feel extraordinary, yet the one who persists finds that extraordinary grace may descend quietly.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
444 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (These nights refine sincerity. They soften the ego. They teach the believer that nearness is not claimed but sought, not assumed but pleaded for. The heart that stands in prostration at three in the morning, whispering quietly in hope and fear, experiences a form of intimacy that cannot be replicated in public worship. In these nights, the believer learns to value solitude with Allah over applause before the community.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<<
