/P 198 0 R
/T (Another sign is discomfort with previous heedlessness. If sins that once felt light now feel heavy, if gatherings that once felt normal now feel distracting, if time wasted now feels regrettable, then purification has begun. The heart that was illuminated by Ramadan cannot return entirely to darkness without resistance.)
/E (Another sign is discomfort with previous heedlessness. If sins that once felt light now feel heavy, if gatherings that once felt normal now feel distracting, if time wasted now feels regrettable, then purification has begun. The heart that was illuminated by Ramadan cannot return entirely to darkness without resistance.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 198 0 R
/T (Ramadan also teaches the believer to measure success differently. The world measures success by accumulation, visibility, and productivity. Ramadan measures success by sincerity, restraint, and remembrance. The one who leaves the month more conscious of Allah, more aware of his own shortcomings, and more dependent upon divine mercy has gained what cannot be quantified.)
/E (Ramadan also teaches the believer to measure success differently. The world measures success by accumulation, visibility, and productivity. Ramadan measures success by sincerity, restraint, and remembrance. The one who leaves the month more conscious of Allah, more aware of his own shortcomings, and more dependent upon divine mercy has gained what cannot be quantified.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 198 0 R
/T (There is also a subtle sign of acceptance in increased humility. If Ramadan produces pride, then its purpose was undermined. If it produces gratitude, then its purpose was fulfilled. The believer who fasted sincerely knows how fragile he is, how easily distracted he becomes, and how dependent he is upon divine aid. This awareness softens judgment toward others and deepens reliance upon Allah.)
/E (There is also a subtle sign of acceptance in increased humility. If Ramadan produces pride, then its purpose was undermined. If it produces gratitude, then its purpose was fulfilled. The believer who fasted sincerely knows how fragile he is, how easily distracted he becomes, and how dependent he is upon divine aid. This awareness softens judgment toward others and deepens reliance upon Allah.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
