/T (Ramadan purifies the one who engages it consciously. It disciplines desire, refines perception, diagnoses disease, magnifies mercy, and reorients longing toward the eternal. The one who enters it heedless and leaves it aware has succeeded. The one who enters it distracted and leaves it reflective has advanced. The one who enters it burdened and leaves it lighter has tasted its secret.)
/E (Ramadan purifies the one who engages it consciously. It disciplines desire, refines perception, diagnoses disease, magnifies mercy, and reorients longing toward the eternal. The one who enters it heedless and leaves it aware has succeeded. The one who enters it distracted and leaves it reflective has advanced. The one who enters it burdened and leaves it lighter has tasted its secret.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [0]
>>
