486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Ramadan benefits the one who enters it with clarity regarding what must not be neglected. Without defined anchors, the month easily dissolves into scattered effort. A believer who desires transformation should establish daily non negotiables that remain constant regardless of fluctuating energy or schedule. The first of these is the preservation of the five daily prayers at their proper times, offered with attentiveness rather than haste. Presence matters more than length, and punctuality disciplines the soul in a way that enthusiasm alone cannot.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
487 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
488 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (The tongue also requires discipline. Ramadan exposes the subtle harm of careless speech, and guarding the tongue becomes one of the most transformative practices of the month. A believer may choose one area of speech to restrain daily, whether it be complaint, argumentation, gossip, or exaggeration. Consistent restraint builds inward strength.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
