546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (Spiritual burnout often occurs when worship becomes competitive rather than contemplative, when comparison replaces sincerity, and when unrealistic goals generate guilt rather than growth. The believer should resist turning Ramadan into a performance before others or before himself. Long nights followed by neglected obligations undermine the very purpose of the month.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
547 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (Balanced effort preserves longevity. Adequate rest, measured recitation, and realistic goals allow the believer to complete the month with steadiness rather than collapse. Social gatherings, while permissible, should not eclipse solitary reflection. Debate over minor matters should not consume spiritual energy. Guarding focus is part of guarding the fast.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (Ramadan is meant to refine the soul, not overwhelm it. Measured discipline sustained across thirty days is more transformative than dramatic intensity sustained for three. The believer who exits Ramadan with stability, and preserved habits has succeeded more than the one who exits exhausted and depleted.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
